(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','jee-main','jee-advanced','comedk','scholarship'],'Chemistry','Class 11-12',2026,'Electrochemistry','','easy','single','In the Daniel cell, the reaction occurring at the anode is:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Zn -> Zn2+ + 2e-"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cu2+ + 2e- -> Cu"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Zn2+ + 2e- -> Zn"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cu -> Cu2+ + 2e-"}]'::jsonb,'"a"'::jsonb,'At the anode, oxidation occurs: Zn(s) -> Zn2+(aq) + 2e-.','["Define anode (oxidation site).", "Identify the more reactive metal (Zn)."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Chemistry XII, Ch 3'),
