(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Breathing and Exchange of Gases','','medium','single','A person who has migrated to a high altitude (above 3500m) will experience ''Altitude Sickness''. Which of the following physiological changes occurs as an adaptation after a few days?','[{"id": "a", "text": "Decreased RBC production and increased hemoglobin binding affinity."}, {"id": "b", "text": "Increased breathing rate and increased hemoglobin binding affinity."}, {"id": "c", "text": "Increased RBC production and decreased hemoglobin binding affinity."}, {"id": "d", "text": "Decreased breathing rate and increased RBC production."}]'::jsonb,'"c"'::jsonb,'Low oxygen at high altitudes triggers increased RBC production and decreased binding affinity of hemoglobin to release O2 to tissues.','["Identify the body''s response to low pO2.", "Recall that high altitude shifts the dissociation curve to the right.", "Select the option reflecting physiological compensation."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XI Ch 17 & XII Ch 13'),
(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Body Fluids and Circulation','','medium','single','In the context of the human cardiac cycle, if the stroke volume is 70 mL and the heart rate is 80 beats per minute, what is the volume of blood pumped by the left ventricle in 30 seconds?','[{"id": "a", "text": "2800 mL"}, {"id": "b", "text": "5600 mL"}, {"id": "c", "text": "4200 mL"}, {"id": "d", "text": "1400 mL"}]'::jsonb,'"a"'::jsonb,'Cardiac output = Stroke Volume x Heart Rate = 70 x 80 = 5600 mL/min. In 30 seconds, it is 2800 mL.','["Calculate Cardiac Output per minute: 70 x 80 = 5600.", "Divide by 2 for 30 seconds.", "Final answer: 2800 mL."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XI Ch 18'),
