(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Principles of Inheritance and Variation','','easy','single','A person with blood group ''AB'' is considered a universal recipient because they have:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Both A and B antigens on RBCs but no antibodies in plasma"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Both A and B antibodies in plasma but no antigens on RBCs"}, {"id": "c", "text": "No antigens on RBCs and no antibodies in plasma"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Antigen A on RBCs and antibody b in plasma"}]'::jsonb,'"a"'::jsonb,'AB group individuals have both A and B antigens on RBCs but no antibodies in the plasma.','["Recall ABO blood grouping system.", "AB group has I^A and I^B alleles.", "No antibodies (anti-A or anti-B) are present in plasma."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XII Ch 5'),
(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Molecular Basis of Inheritance','','easy','single','The ''Central Dogma'' of molecular biology was proposed by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "James Watson"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Maurice Wilkins"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Rosalind Franklin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Francis Crick"}]'::jsonb,'"d"'::jsonb,'Francis Crick proposed the Central Dogma, which states that genetic information flows from DNA to RNA to Protein.','["Identify the scientist associated with Central Dogma."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XII Ch 6'),
