(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Evolution','','easy','single','The theory of evolution by natural selection was given by:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Lamarck"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Hugo de Vries"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Charles Darwin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Thomas Malthus"}]'::jsonb,'"c"'::jsonb,'Charles Darwin proposed that variations which are heritable and make resource utilization better will lead to survival and reproduction.','["Identify evolutionary theorists.", "Lamarck: Use/Disuse. De Vries: Mutations. Darwin: Natural Selection."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XII Ch 7'),
(ARRAY['kcet','neet-ug','scholarship'],'Zoology','Class 11-12',2026,'Evolution','','easy','single','Analogous structures are a result of:','[{"id": "a", "text": "Convergent evolution"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Divergent evolution"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Genetic drift"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Adaptive radiation"}]'::jsonb,'"a"'::jsonb,'Analogous organs evolve due to similar selection pressures in different lineages, leading to convergent evolution.','["Define analogy vs homology.", "Analogy = different origin, same function (Convergent)."]'::jsonb,'Original NCERT-aligned question — Study at Bangalore (AI-assisted draft, pending teacher review)',false,'verified','NCERT Biology XII Ch 7'),
